Given that:
(i) direct generation is applied in language processing, so variants of diffusion modeling do handle variable length inputs;
(ii) the paper is extra defensive on the benefits of UV and would not admit the drawbacks of this as a representation;
(iii) comparisons with FAM benchmark being seemingly disadvantageous for FAM;
(iv) the revised version did not include some of my suggestions or some of the discussion mentioned, and does not cite the literature;

I prefer to keep my original rating. Additionally, while subjective, simply extending autoregressive modeling to seam generation does not provide me an interesting insight.
